The '''Pininfarina Battista''' is an electric performance car manufactured by [[Automobili Pininfarina]] GmbH which is headquartered in [[Munich]], [[Germany]], with roots in the Italian car design firm and coachbuilder [[Pininfarina]]. The name Battista is a tribute to Pininfarina's founder [[Battista Pininfarina]].<ref name=":0" /> The car was publicly unveiled at the [[Geneva Motor Show#2019|2019 Geneva Motor Show]]. It is the first Pininfarina-branded car.

==Specifications and features==
[[File:2019 Automobili Pininfarina Battista Rear.jpg|thumb|Rear view]]

The Battista is powered by a 120&nbsp;kW⋅h battery pack supplied by [[Rimac Automobili]]. The car has four individual motors, each placed at a wheel, and they have a combined power output of 1400&nbsp;kW and 2300 N⋅m of torque.

The car has a carbon fibre monocoque [[chassis]] with aluminium crash structures at the front and rear. Most of the body panels are also built from the same material resulting in a low mass. The car has 21" rims in [[Pirelli]] P Zero Corsa tyres.

The adjustable suspension system of the car will be tuned for maximum road comfort. The car has five driving modes all of which alter the power generated by the powertrain. The car features carbon ceramic brake discs measuring 390&nbsp;mm at the front and rear and is equipped with six-piston calipers front and aft. The active rear wing acts as an airbrake to improve stopping power.

The interior of the car is customisable according to the customer's specifications. A carbon fibre steering wheel is flanked by two large screens on either side, displaying vital data to the driver. The interior is upholstered in leather. The car is claimed by the manufacturer to generate cabin driving sound using acoustics.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://newatlas.com/pininfarina-battista-electric-hypercar/58727/|title=Pininfarina Battista unveiled: 1 400 kW electric hypercar is an absolute stunner|date=5 March 2019|first=Loz|last=Blain|publisher=New Atlas|access-date=6 March 2019}}</ref>

The battery pack is T-shaped and is placed so that it lies in the central tunnel and behind the seats. Once fully charged, the battery pack allows the car to have a range of 450&nbsp;km.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://techcrunch.com/2019/03/05/pininfarinas-2-million-electric-battista-hypercar-is-faster-than-a-formula-1-race-car/|title=Pininfarina's $2 million electric 'Battista' hypercar is faster than a Formula 1 race car|date=5 March 2019|first=Kristen|last=Korosec|publisher=Tech Crunch|access-date=6 March 2019}}</ref>

==Performance==
The Battista accelerates from 0 to 100&nbsp;km/h in 1.89 seconds, 0 to 300&nbsp;km/h in 10.49 seconds, and has a top speed of 358.03&nbsp;km/h (222 MPH).<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Pininfarina Battista achieves a top speed of 358kmph at Natrax test facility, sets new record |url=https://www.financialexpress.com/auto/car-news/pininfarina-battista-achieves-a-top-speed-of-358kmph-at-natrax-test-facility-sets-new-record/2990699/ |access-date=2023-02-24 |website=Financialexpress |date=23 February 2023 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-02-23 |title=Pininfarina Battista sets new Indian land speed record |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/sports/others/pininfarina-battista-sets-new-indian-land-speed-record-101677171900026.html |access-date=2023-02-24 |website=Hindustan Times |language=en}}</ref>

==Production==
Production of the Battista began in 2022, with a limit of 150 units.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tudose |first=Sergiu |date=2022-07-13 |title=Pininfarina Battista Electric Hyper GT Enters Series Production at Cambiano R&D Hub |url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/pininfarina-battista-electric-hyper-gt-enters-series-production-at-cambiano-r-d-hub-193424.html |access-date=2022-07-13 |website=autoevolution |language=en}}</ref> The units will be equally allocated among prospective buyers from [[North America]], [[Europe]], [[Asia]] and [[Middle East]]. Each car is hand-built at the dedicated Pininfarina facility located in [[Cambiano]], [[Italy]]. 40 percent of the car's production was already reserved before the car's introduction.<ref name="electrek">{{cite web|url=https://electrek.co/2019/03/05/pininfarina-battista-electric-hypercar/|title=Pininfarina Battista is a 1,900 horsepower all-electric car|date=5 March 2019|first=Phil|last=Deziky|publisher=Electrek|access-date=6 March 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cnbc.com/2019/03/05/pininfarina-battista-2-million-all-electric-car-is-worlds-fastest.html|title=A new $2 million all-electric 'hypercar' accelerates faster than an F-16 jet|date=5 March 2019|first=David|last=Reid|publisher=[[CNBC]]|access-date=6 March 2019}}</ref>

In June 2019, Automobili Pininfarina unveiled a revised version of the Battista performance car in [[Turin]], Italy. The new design elements come as the model advances through its development programme, towards the simulation, wind tunnel and development drive stages. Changes made to the design include a more aggressive front end and revised wing mirrors having stalks similar to [[LaFerrari]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.evo.co.uk/news/22047/automobili-pininfarina-battista-shown-in-italy-with-new-design-tweaks|title=Automobili Pininfarina Battista shown in Italy with new design tweaks|date=20 June 2019|first=Jordan|last=Katsianis|publisher=[[Evo (magazine)|Evo]]|accessdate=22 June 2019}}</ref>

=== Battista Anniversario ===
[[File:Pininfarina Battista Anniversario.jpg|thumb|Battista Anniversario]]
On 22 May 2020 Automobili Pininfarina unveiled a special edition of the Battista called the Anniversario. Each Battista Anniversario is hand-painted in Cambiano. The car needs to be disassembled and reassembled three times before it obtains its final livery.<ref>{{Citation|title=A Tribute to the 90th Anniversary of Pininfarina – This Is Battista Anniversario|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-WCa0AhXp6A|language=en|access-date=2021-09-14}}</ref> The colour scheme is an homage to the Piedmont environment, where Battista "Pinin" Farina worked and lived: Bianco Setriere, Grigio Antonelliano, and the Pininfarina signature colour, the Iconica Blu. To go alongside the new color scheme Automobili Pininfarina created a new wheel design: the Impulso. These centre-lock forged aluminium wheels represent an upgrade not only in aesthetics but also in car performance, thanks to a 10-kilo weight reduction compared to Battista wheels. The rear pair has been enlarged from 20-inch to 21-inch to enable greater traction when driving in high-performance environments.

The Battista Anniversario features a set of aerodynamic enhancements in a set called the "Furiosa Package" this includes: A carbon fibre front splitter, side blades and a rear diffuser that work together to grant increased downforce and improved stability at high cornering speeds.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Battista Anniversario: the hypercar of the future {{!}} Pininfarina|url=https://www.automobili-pininfarina.com/battista-anniversario|access-date=2021-09-14|website=www.automobili-pininfarina.com|language=en}}</ref>

=== Battista Nino Farina===
Battista Edizione Nino Farina is a limited edition of just 5 vehicles, named after [[Giuseppe Farina|Giuseppe "Nino" Farina]] a first [[Formula One]] World Champion and a nephew of [[Battista Pininfarina]]. This edition debuted at the 2023 Goodwood Festival of Speed.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/electric/pininfarina-battista-edizione-nino-farina-ps32m-limited-edition-ev-hypercar|title=The Pininfarina Battista Edizione Nino Farina is a £3.2m limited edition EV hypercar|website=topgear.com|access-date=18 February 2024}}</ref>

=== Battista Targamerica ===
Battista Targamerica is a one-off, open top variant of the Battista. It was commissioned by [[Michael Jordan]] and features a roof-less design, unique five-spoke wheel design and a custom aluminum and glass cigar humidor. Targamerica is the very first coachbuilt one-off special with livery inspired by the [[Ferrari Testarossa#Testarossa Spider|Ferrari Testarossa Spider]] of [[Gianni Agnelli]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.autoevolution.com/news/michael-jordan-is-the-mystery-owner-of-the-only-battista-targamerica-in-the-world-240854.html|title=Michael Jordan Is the Mystery Owner of the Only Battista Targamerica in the World|website=autoevolution.com|access-date=8 October 2024}}</ref>

